                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "🚌 Well, I'll never forgive this game for its wasted concept. Just look at the promo art, it's stunning, but the game is abandoned shovelware. The main problem is the clunky implementation of everything, as well as the NEED for an online connection for solo play and even customization. Hit detection is terrible, there is no impact from hits or even taken damage. Animations are constantly glitching. The balance is broken, it's easy, but you can be cornered and lose in the blink of an eye. Only two classes (with useless abilities) and six similar missions in small school arenas (~2h). Enemies seem different, but they behave the same. The final boss is a sponge with broken hitboxes. Multiplayer is in perpetual beta. The shop interface is buggy. The selection of outfit elements is poor (as well as colors) and making individual items shades as paid DLCs is ridiculous. Cheap but disappointing, and I played it longer than it deserved.",
